\begin_layout Point
Combining this theorem with Lemma 1 and the Computable Completeness Theorem,
 we get:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Point
Theorem (Pakhomov):
 There is a theory which is definitionally equivalent to PA and admits computable nonstandard models.
\end_layout

\begin_layout point
Proof:
 The theory is 
\begin_inset Formula $T_{S}$
\end_inset

.
 It is definitionally equivalent to PA by Lemma 1.
 Add to it some axiom or axiom schema that ensures nonstandard,
 say 
\begin_inset Formula $T^{+}$
\end_inset

.
 Use CCT to get a 
\begin_inset Formula $0'$
\end_inset

-computable model 
\begin_inset Formula $(M,\in,S)$
\end_inset

 of 
\begin_inset Formula $T^{+}$
\end_inset

plus def.
 of 
\begin_inset Formula $\in$
\end_inset

.
 The reduct 
\begin_inset Formula $(M,S)$
\end_inset

 is thus a nonstandard model of 
\begin_inset Formula $T_{S}$
\end_inset

,
